Expectations of the native link's tests (tests/native-link.scala). The program is the one of
tests/nir/fixtures (tests/nir/src/Shapes.scala, main class fix.Shapes), linked for the target
x86_64-unknown-linux-musl against the jars of Scala Native 0.5.12 that tests/nir/digests.txt names,
the program's directory first on the class path and the jars after it in that file's order.

digests.txt   the SHA-256 and the lines of what Scala Native's own tools (tools_3 0.5.12) leave for
              that class path and main class in a debug build with the immix collector and its
              optimizer off, once as the build decides on threads (it links without them: the
              program starts none) and once told to link with them:
                linked   the definitions its link reaches, as its build dumps them (`dump`,
                         linked.hnir): each as nir.Show prints it, in the order of the names
              They are Scala Native's bytes, never teq's: `teq nir --link` has to print the same.
linked.txt    of the first link's dump, the definitions of the classes tests/native-link.scala
              names, whole and as they stand there: what a failure is read against
entries.txt   the names Scala Native's build gives its link to start from (`ScalaNative.entries`)
              for that main class, without threads and with them, in its list's order: the order
              teq's link reaches them in (src/native/reach.rs's tests)
scala-collections.txt
              the hashCode of names, paths and positions and the iteration order of the Scala
              library's mutable.HashSet and mutable.HashMap after generated operations, as Scala
              Native's classes and scala-library 3.8.4 give them on the JVM: the tables teq's link
              keeps where Scala Native's iterates one (src/native/scala.rs's tests; its header
              says more)
diamond/      a diamond of traits linked at many depths, Scala Native's listings up to the depth its
              link ends at and teq's own past it (its README)

The expectations are remade by running Scala Native's tools on the JVM over the same class path
(`scala.scalanative.build.Build.build` with `withDump(true)`, `withOptimize(false)`, `GC.immix`,
`Mode.debug`, the target triple and, for the second link, `withMultithreading(true)`), and by
taking the lines of the named classes out of linked.hnir for linked.txt; entries.txt and
scala-collections.txt by programs that call Scala Native's classes and the Scala library's on the
JVM. No file here is written from teq's output, but for the two digests of diamond/digests.txt
that name teq (diamond/README says why).
